  "description": "WEGLEC crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C60 H96 Er8 Ge12 N4 O64,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er1B (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2B (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er3B (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er4B (Er) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.710-3.747 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 108.99-110.43°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C60H100Er8Ge12N4O66. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 24 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 16 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
